    q: 'Is an MBA in business analytics good for engineers?',
    a: 'Yes, especially for CSE, IT, ECE, and EEE engineers. It typically offers freshers Rs 6-10 LPA, with average placements at top IIMs in the Rs 15-32 LPA range. Roles like data scientist, analytics manager, and strategy consultant reward the combination of engineering-grade quantitative skill with business framing that an MBA adds. The main gate is your comfort with SQL, statistics, and translating numbers into a business decision, not your specific engineering stream.',
