    q: 'Do I need CAT or can engineers use GATE for MBA admission?',
    a: 'CAT (Common Admission Test), not GATE, is the primary entrance exam accepted by IIMs and most top B-schools for MBA admission. GATE is designed for MTech and other postgraduate engineering admissions, and while a small number of institutes accept it as a supplementary criterion, it is not a substitute for CAT if IIMs or top-tier MBA programs are your goal. Other accepted exams include XAT, GMAT, CMAT, and MAT depending on the institute.',
